# coq-hook-page.service - the page: runs when coq-hook-listener.service or coq-hook-forward.service exhausts its restarts.
# It posts one blocked 423 record to the orchestrator (events/bin/event.sh add --kind blocked --code 423 --seat hook-listener
# --to orchestrator --note "<unit> failed 3 restarts"), which factory/config/routes.json already escalates to the architect and then
# the owner page. systemd gives an OnFailure= unit MONITOR_UNIT, the failed unit's name, and hook-listener.sh page reads it.
# It is a record and not a message to a pane: nothing here needs a pane to be alive.
# Install once, as the owner or orchestrator: systemctl --user link <checkout>/line/units/coq-hook-page.service
[Unit]
Description=Coq hook page: tell the orchestrator a hook unit is down

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=%h/projects/coq-jev-herdr-plugin/line/bin/hook-listener.sh page
